<title>USA: U.S. factory lard use - Census.</title>
<headline>U.S. factory lard use - Census.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. factories used 32.0 million lbs of lard in edible and inedible product output in August 1996 versus a revised 32.5 million lbs in July and 35.9 million lbs in August 1995 the Census Bureau said.</p>
<p>Usage so far in the 1996 period amounted to 281.3 million lbs versus 307.1 million lbs in the 1995 period.</p>
<p>Usage includes hydrogenated vegetable and animal fats and other fats and oils in process.</p>
